    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">793</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raid on the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a> opens the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 965</span><span class="rf-text">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-bluetooth">Harald Bluetooth</a> raises the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jelling">Jelling</a> stone, recording that he made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> Christian</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1000</span><span class="rf-text">The Icelandic assembly, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/althing">Althing</a>, adopts <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, allowing pagan worship in private for a time</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1075</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-of-bremen">Adam of Bremen</a> describes the temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a> with images of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Thor</a>, Odin and Freyr</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1220</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/snorri-sturluson">Snorri Sturluson</a> writes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edda">Prose Edda</a>, a handbook of Norse myth and poetry</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1270</span><span class="rf-text">The Codex Regius, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edda">Poetic Edda</a>, is written in Iceland</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1973</span><span class="rf-text">Iceland recognises the modern Ásatrú fellowship as a religion</span></li></ol>
    </section>

